# Trivy suppression file for the ModelOps serving image.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line. `#` starts a comment.
# Trivy will not fail the build on CVEs listed here.
#
# EVERY entry below must be re-evaluated when the base image is updated.
# The workflow pins the base digest, so a new digest is a deliberate action
# that should be accompanied by a fresh triage of this file.
#
# Context:
# - The base is python:3.12-slim (Debian 13.7 "trixie").
# - The application runs as a non-root user (UID 1001) with no shell and no
#   login privileges. Container escape via these CVEs would need to first
#   defeat that, and then exploit an OS package the app never invokes.
# - 0 CVEs were found in any Python package, including scikit-learn, numpy,
#   pandas, mlflow, fastapi, pydantic, and their transitive dependencies.
# - All findings are in Debian 13 OS packages with no fix currently published.
#   When Debian publishes patches, a base-image digest update will pick them
#   up and this list must shrink.

# POLICY (updated 2026-10-12): the scan runs with --ignore-unfixed.
# CVEs without a published fix are allowed automatically. This file
# additionally suppresses specific CVEs that DO have fixes but have
# been triaged as not exploitable in our runtime. If Debian publishes
# a fix, the corresponding entry must be removed from this file so the
# gate can validate the upgrade.

# ── util-linux family (mount, bsdutils, login, libblkid1, libmount1, etc.) ──
# The app never invokes any util-linux binary. The CVE affects external
# mount helpers and nsenter cgroup migration; neither is reachable at runtime.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# ── curl / libcurl4t64 ──
# curl is installed solely to satisfy the container HEALTHCHECK and entrypoint
# readiness loop against a trusted local MLflow server. The HTTP requests our
# code issues never use SSH, SFTP, SCP, or proxy authentication (the affected
# code paths), so these CVEs are unreachable.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8458
CVE-2026-8927

# ── libgnutls30t64 ──
# gnutls is a transitive dependency of curl. Our HTTPS traffic is either to
# PyPI during image build (from inside the builder stage, not the runtime
# image) or to our own MLflow server over plain HTTP. No external TLS
# handshakes happen at runtime.
CVE-2026-88647
CVE-2026-88648

# ── libacl1 ──
# The CVE requires the app to call libacl symlink-handling APIs. The app does
# not link against libacl directly and does not manipulate ACLs.
CVE-2026-54369

# ── ncurses ──
# ncurses is present for Debian base tooling (e.g., dpkg). The runtime image
# does not open a TTY, does not run interactive programs, and does not
# process untrusted terminal escape sequences.
CVE-2025-69720

# ── systemd / libsystemd0 / libudev1 ──
# systemd-homed is not installed. The library is present because Debian base
# tooling links against it, but the vulnerable code path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-16742

# ── perl-base ──
# Debian 13 has marked this as fix_deferred. perl-base is a base-image
# dependency (used by dpkg). The app does not invoke Perl or process untrusted
# tar archives.
CVE-2026-9538
